  "chapter": {
    "number": 107,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(108) Song of a Psalm by David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God, my heart is ready, my heart is ready; I will sing and sing psalms with my glory.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Awake, lute and harp; I will awake early.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give thanks to you, O Lord, among the people; I will sing praise to you among the Gentiles.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your mercy is great above the heavens, and your truth reaches to the clouds.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you exalted, O God, above the heavens; and your glory above all the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "That your beloved ones may be delivered, save with your right hand, and hear me. God has spoken in his sanctuary;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will be exalted, and will divide Sicima, and will measure out the valley of tents.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Galaad is mine; and Manasses is mine; and Ephraim is the help of my head; Judas is my king;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Moab is the caldron of my hope; over Idumea will I cast my sandal; the Philistines are made subject to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Who will bring me into the fortified city? or who will guide me to Idumea?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Will not you, O God, who have rejected us? and will not you, O God, go forth with our hosts?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Give us help from tribulation: for vain is the help of man.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Through God we shall",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 205
          },
          {
            "text": "do valiantly; and he will bring to nothing our enemies.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 205,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. work power.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 107,
          "verse": 13
        }
      }
    ]
